 R←Test_API_037(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;buff;log;res;parms
⍝ Runs "Log" with -commit= and with -name= against a folder that is NOT an opened project.
⍝ * -commit= compared the user's hash against the whole line, and the default format carries the
⍝   SHORT hash, so a full 40-character hash - what every other Git tool hands you - never matched
⍝   and the filter was silently skipped.
⍝ * -name= was resolved with `space`, which is empty for a plain path, so <IdentifyObject> went
⍝   looking in whatever project happened to be open.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 log←tempDir G.Log tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2>≢log

 ⍝ The FULL hash of the second-newest commit:
 (rc msg buff)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'rev-parse HEAD~1'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp 40≠≢∊buff
 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.commit←∊buff
 res←parms G.Log tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp(≢res)≥≢log               ⍝ Something must have been filtered out

 ⍝ -name= must be resolved in THIS project, not in an open one
 parms←⎕NS''
 parms.name←'Counter.aplf'   ⍝ Not an open project, so it must be the file name
 res←parms G.Log tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp 3≠≢res                   ⍝ Counter.aplf was changed by three commits

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
